// The registers of the graphics block (GCA, GFX 8.0) of the Radeon RX 580
// (Polaris 10) as Linux v6.6 has them. GENERATED by
// tools/gpu_registers_generate.py (do not edit: generate it again; README.md
// beside it says how a register is added) from
// drivers/gpu/drm/amd/include/asic_reg/gca/gfx_8_0_d.h and
// gca/gfx_8_0_sh_mask.h and gca/gfx_8_0_enum.h, whose sha256 are
//   gfx_8_0_d.h       299228e0bbd75d0f5879efbaea0234793fa77dece92646efe6adb6f5f9832a4a
//   gfx_8_0_sh_mask.h c2dd6e2f68a047114578ed48de852fcc02fae4c07dada7ef03fa89a6cde1cc85
//   gfx_8_0_enum.h    fa6b8ff974fccdd54aa0e1b6a6430508a558fd263ead90eaf70bef262e4d5d63
//
// 137 of the header's 2800 registers, the ones SELECTION names and the 32
// the database has in another form (gfx8.mlx's head names them), each with
// every field the header gives it (651 fields), and 4 of gfx_8_0_enum.h's
// enums. A register is its number as Linux and the kernel count it, the
// dword index of its MMIO word (the header's mmNAME without "mm"; a register
// of an index space keeps the header's "ix"). NAME__FIELD is a field's mask,
// NAME__FIELD__SHIFT its lowest bit; an enum is a struct of its values.

